01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:33,500
(stylised W./E.) is a 2011 historical romantic drama film written and directed by Madonna and
starring Abbie Cornish, Andrea Riseborough, Oscar Isaac, Richard Coyle, and James D'Arcy.

14
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:31,000
The screenplay was co-written by Alek Keshishian, who previously worked with Madonna
on her 1991 documentary Truth or Dare and two of her music videos.

15
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
Although the film was panned by critics and was a box office bomb, it
received an Academy Award nomination for Best Costume Design.

16
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
This marked Isaac's and Cornish's second film together after Sucker Punch.

17
01:24:17,500 --> 01:24:23,500
The film tells the story of two women separated by over six decades.

18
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
In 1998, lonely New Yorker Wally Winthrop is obsessed with Edward VIII's abdication
of the British throne so he could marry American Wallis Simpson.

19
01:34:12,500 --> 01:34:18,500
But Wally's research, including several visits to Sotheby's auction of the Windsor estate,
reveals that the couple's life together was not as perfect as she thought.

20
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
Traveling back and forth in time, W.E.

21
01:44:07,500 --> 01:44:13,500
intertwines Wally's journey of discovery in New York with the story of Wallis and Edward from the
early days of their romance to the unraveling of their lives over the following decades.

22
01:49:05,000 --> 01:49:11,000
The film explores themes of auction, beating, bathtub, clothes, woman director.

23
01:54:02,500 --> 01:54:08,500
The tone is emotional.
